speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to the provisions of Standing Order 43, I request the unanimous consent of the House to move a motion concerning an important and urgent matter.

May 5, 1977
Oral Questions
Whereas Air Canada has recently adopted a new passenger schedule by which citizens of the central Maritime area, which includes southeastern New Brunswick and northwestern Nova Scotia, have been given the worst air passenger schedule ever presented for at least the last 20 years;
And whereas Air Canada flights in and out of Moncton for Montreal and Ottawa have been literally stripped of any convenience to the travelling public causing a deplorable result on already fragile economic conditions and will have devastating effects on the upcoming tourist industry;
And whereas some of the flights on the new Air Canada schedule necessitate a stopover in Montreal of approximately two to three hours;
I move, seconded by the hon. member for Cumberland-Col-chester North (Mr. Coates):
That the Minister of Transport immediately take steps to insist that Air Canada revise the recently adopted passenger schedule to provide a more convenient, useful and practical service from Ottawa-Montreal-Moncton and return for the use of passengers in the central Maritime region.
